        "findings": [
          {
            "scope": "Excess Charge ordinary and ordinary-bottom captures",
            "result": "All three ranks are readable in the ordinary window: 0.67, 1.34 and 2.01 shielding per effective level of the imbued wand. The last paragraph visibly includes temporary wand-level bonuses, rounding to the nearest whole shield point, and retaining a stronger existing Barrier instead of adding amounts. The whole ordinary body fits the viewport; the normal-bottom capture remains readable with the Show calculations control below it."
          },
          {
            "scope": "Excess Charge expanded and expanded-bottom captures",
            "result": "The expanded section shows current rank 2/3, round(effective wand level x 0.67 x rank), the 1.34 rank-two factor, and the effective imbued-wand level distinction. The bottom view includes stronger Barrier retention, no hidden-level revelation, and usual time/charge consumption, with its final line visible above Hide calculations. The intermediate expanded view has a partial preceding-text fragment at the top edge of the scroll viewport; the bottom view makes the final text fully reachable. No final-line obstruction or inaccessible description was observed."
          },
          {
            "scope": "Counter Ability ordinary and ordinary-bottom captures",
            "result": "The normal window visibly lists all four ranks as 0.38, 0.75, 1.13 and 1.5 charges. Rank two shows 0.75, not 0.77. The final rank and its last charges line are completely visible with bottom padding. No calculation section, raw formatting placeholder or final-line clipping appears in these two captures."
          },
          {
            "scope": "Trap On, restarted and Off captures",
            "result": "All three screenshots now show the actual Continue when traps are revealed row and its help. On and the fresh-process restarted view visibly show a checked control; Off visibly shows an unchecked control. The previous offscreen-row capture limitation is corrected for these APD441 images."
          },
          {
            "scope": "Trap runtime Ooze capture",
            "result": "The synthetic fixture image contains the gameplay HUD, a dark offset dungeon view and the floor-entry message. No readable Caustic ooze message or visible effect on the hero can be established from this frame. The passing gameplay report supports the runtime assertions; this image alone does not visually prove the Ooze effect, movement sequence or a natural generated-room route."
          },
          {
            "scope": "Four wall captures",
            "result": "The magenta searched-face mark is visible at the eligible wall and remains in the lifecycle capture. The corner and doorway captures have no stale mark at the fixture. All four original images were viewed at full size."
          },
          {
            "scope": "Five inventory captures",
            "result": "Backpack, Magical Holster, Potion Bandolier and Velvet Pouch contents, quantity/upgrade labels and bag controls are visible. The final Backpack view remains readable. No clipped inventory control or broken glyph was observed. Ordering semantics are supported by the native assertions rather than established solely from screenshots."
          }
